<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="{{ site.csp }}">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
{% if emst.release.isPreview %}<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">{% endif %}
<meta name="description" content="{{ description or 'EMST Explorer: how environmental jobs are changing, local-first gap check, exploratory pathways. Generated from an EMST release build.' }}">
<meta name="emst-release" content="{{ emst.release.id }}">
<title>{{ title }} · EMST Explorer · {{ emst.release.id }}</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/vendor/uswds/css/uswds.min.css' | url }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/emst.css' | url }}">
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/emst.js' | url }}"></script>
</head>
<body>
<a class="usa-skipnav" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>
<div class="emst-release-banner" role="region" aria-label="Release and use notice">
  <div class="emst-wrap">
    <p><strong>Release {{ emst.release.id }}{% if emst.release.isPreview %} · draft for NGO-pilot preview, not a release{% endif %}.</strong>
    {% if emst.release.isPreview %}Every record here is a draft, mostly written by AI agents, and has not yet been reviewed by independent human experts.{% endif %}
    For development and planning only; not a selection instrument.</p>
    {% if emst.release.warning %}<p><strong>Build warning:</strong> {{ emst.release.warning }}</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
<header class="emst-header">
  <div class="emst-wrap">
    <p class="emst-header__title"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">EMST Explorer</a></p>
    <p class="emst-header__sub">Environmental Management Skills Taxonomy: how environmental jobs are changing</p>
    <nav class="emst-nav" aria-label="Main">
      <ul>
        {% set navItems = [
          ["/", "Home"], ["/roles/", "Roles"], ["/gap-check/", "Gap check"], ["/pathways/", "Pathways"],
          ["/whats-coming/", "What's coming"], ["/federal-series/", "Federal series"], ["/state-classes/", "State and local classes"],
          ["/competencies/", "Competencies"], ["/evidence/", "Evidence"], ["/search/", "Search"]
        ] %}
        {% for item in navItems %}
        {% set active = (page.url == item[0]) or (item[0] != "/" and page.url.startsWith(item[0])) %}
        <li><a href="{{ item[0] | url }}"{% if active %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item[1] }}</a></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
<div class="emst-wrap">
  {% if crumbs %}
  <nav class="emst-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol>
    <li><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">Home</a></li>
    {% for c in crumbs %}<li>{% if c[0] %}<a href="{{ c[0] | url }}">{{ c[1] }}</a>{% else %}<span aria-current="page">{{ c[1] }}</span>{% endif %}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ol></nav>
  {% endif %}
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
{{ content | safe }}
  </main>
</div>
<footer class="emst-footer">
  <div class="emst-wrap">
    <p><strong>Release {{ emst.release.id }}</strong> · profile <code>{{ emst.release.profile }}</code> · schema {{ emst.release.schemaVersion }} · released {{ emst.release.date }} · build <code>{{ emst.release.buildCommit }}</code> · display gates {{ emst.release.gatesVersion }} (release view stamped {{ emst.release.displayGateRule }}; the explorer applies the role-profile rules of {{ emst.release.gatesVersion }} itself) · use tiers {{ emst.release.eutRule }}</p>
    <p>{{ emst.release.notice }}</p>
    <p data-emst-policy="indigenous-statement">{{ emst.release.indigenousStatement }} Content under the project's Tribal content hold is excluded from every build until a Tribal Advisory Council approves it. These pages neither show nor describe it; the release notes give only a count of held records.</p>
    <p><strong>Who made this.</strong> This explorer and its records were researched and drafted by a team of AI agents (Anthropic's Claude), each given a specialist role, working to a charter set by the EMST project lead. AI agents checked the facts against sources in October 2026. No independent human expert has reviewed it yet. Role names such as "Chief Taxonomy Architect", or "EMST's federal HR agent" on these pages, are AI agent roles, not people.</p>
    <p>To comment, correct an error or ask about the pilot, open an issue at <a class="emst-url" href="https://github.com/jrwashebek/Enviroskillstaxonomy/issues" rel="noreferrer">github.com/jrwashebek/Enviroskillstaxonomy/issues</a> (GitHub is a third-party site; this explorer sends nothing itself).</p>
    <p>This explorer runs entirely in your browser. It sets no cookies, keeps no logs, loads nothing from other websites and sends nothing you enter anywhere. <a href="{{ '/about/privacy/' | url }}">What we do not collect</a>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="{{ '/about/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ '/about/accessibility/' | url }}">Accessibility</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ '/about/security/' | url }}">Security</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ '/download/' | url }}">Download and cite</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ '/challenge/' | url }}">Challenge a judgment</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ '/evidence/' | url }}">How to read the evidence</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Data and standard text: CC0 1.0. Explorer code: Apache-2.0. Built with the U.S. Web Design System (USWDS 3) design tokens and components; this is not a U.S. government website.</p>
  </div>
</footer>
{% for s in scripts or [] %}<script src="{{ s | url }}" defer></script>
{% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
